-------------------------------------------------------------------
Thu Sep 24 15:32:28 UTC 2026 - Yunhe Guo <i@guoyunhe.me>

- Update to 0.16.0:
  * YAML compliance: 100% success rate on the YAML test suite, both
    for valid and invalid cases; parse errors are now raised for many
    previously accepted invalid documents
  * improve tracking of the node causing a deserialization error
  * add serialization to/from Tree, not only NodeRef/ConstNodeRef
  * deprecate .to_val() and the operators =, |=, <<, >> in favour of
    the new set_*(), set_serialized() and deserialize() methods, see
    the upstream migration guide
  * the c4core submodule was removed; only the required c4core source
    code is vendored into ryml and is built into libryml
  * see https://github.com/biojppm/rapidyaml/releases/tag/v0.16.0
- Bump the soname to libryml.so.0.16, rename the libryml0_8_0
  subpackage to libryml0_16
- Drop the libc4core0_2_5 subpackage, c4core is no longer built as a
  separate library
- Drop cmake.patch: installing into CMAKE_INSTALL_LIBDIR is fixed
  upstream (biojppm/rapidyaml#256)

-------------------------------------------------------------------
Tue Mar  4 19:14:51 UTC 2025 - Andreas Stieger <andreas.stieger@gmx.de>

- update to 0.8.0 (boo#1238562):
  * deserialization bug fixes
  * portability improvements
  * add handling of Byte Order Marks
  * fix emit of explicit keys when indented
- includes changes from 0.7.2:
  * fix test failures with g++14 -O2 in ppc64le
- includes changes from 0.7.1:
  * Add version functions and macros
- includes changes from 0.7.0:
  * parser refactoring
  * append-emitting to existing containers in the emitrs_ functions
  * add depth query methods
  * add a function to estimate the required tree capacity, based
    on yaml markup
- includes changes from 0.6.0:
  * improved error handling

